GPLv3 Section 5 Modification & Clean-Room Exclusions Notice
-----------------------------------------------------------
`ftxr-core` and `ftxr-modem` are pure-Rust ports derived from WSJT-X's classic
single-threaded FT8 (`lib/ft8/`), FT4 (`lib/ft4/`), and 77-bit (`lib/77bit/`)
implementations, modified for thread-safe session-scoped execution, warm FFT
reuse, parallel candidate decoding with deterministic subtraction ordering, and
standalone CLI/IPC operation.

Non-GPL / third-party routines present in upstream WSJT-X source files are
explicitly excluded from this codebase and replaced with Rust standard library
or clean-room pure-Rust implementations:
  - Unused special-function code in `lib/ft8/ft8b.f90` (excluded entirely)
  - Legacy Fortran index/shell sorting (`lib/indexx.f90`, `lib/shell.f90`),
    replaced with Rust `std` slice sorting (`sort_by`, `sort_unstable_by`,
    `select_nth_unstable_by`)
  - Weighted polynomial fit (`lib/polyfit.f90`, `lib/determ.f90`), replaced
    with clean-room 5x5 ordinary least-squares Gaussian elimination
  - Boost C++ CRC wrapper (`lib/crc14.cpp`), implemented natively in pure Rust

